# PlantUML rendering server.
#
# Read at BUILD time by Vite and inlined into the client bundle, so changing it
# requires a rebuild (`bun run generate`) — setting it at runtime has no effect.
#
# The value's *form* decides when diagrams are rendered:
#
#   - Absolute (http://…) — rendered during prerender and inlined into the HTML,
#     so the published page issues no diagram requests. Used by the Pages deploy
#     workflow, which runs its own PlantUML server as a build service.
#   - Same-origin (/plantuml) — cannot be resolved during prerender, so diagrams
#     render in the browser against that path. Used by the Docker image, where
#     nginx proxies /plantuml/ to the plantuml compose service.
#
# Defaults:
#   - `bun run dev`:  http://localhost:8081 — `bun dev` starts this renderer for you
#                     via `docker compose up -d plantuml`, and reuses one already running.
#   - Docker image:   /plantuml (set via ARG in the Dockerfile).
#
# Point this at a remote server only if you accept the disclosure: the diagram text
# is deflate+base64 encoded into the request URL path, which is trivially
# reversible — that server receives the full source of every diagram it renders.
#
# VITE_PLANTUML_SERVER=https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml
